{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-32027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the matrix\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ find ${B}^{-1}$ by performing row operations." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070268/state.json" "file_sha256" "02a704225abf9ff9e445d2e0b7b7f8c84cc44a0f9c899041ade2c92f26b4add6"} {"question" "q-32027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We consider the augmented matrix $[B\\,|\\,I]$ where $I$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix. Applying the indicated row operations we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  \\\\  & =[I\\,|\\,{B}^{-1}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse matrix is \n\n$$\n{B}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070268/state.json" "file_sha256" "02a704225abf9ff9e445d2e0b7b7f8c84cc44a0f9c899041ade2c92f26b4add6"} {"question" "q-32027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070268/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "286fe9a1c196e3f51f12dbdf4bacd311eb6fddb07e87c07dddb84f75627f44ee"} {"question" "q-32027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answ